        dosage: "Common mistaken: 300–900 mg standardized extract daily 'for mood / anxiety / sleep'", synergies: [],
        gorkipedia: "Gorkipedia Entry (WARNING): St. John's wort is a strong enzyme inducer, not a mild tea. People who take it in place of prescribed medicines have seen those medicines lose effect, including drugs used for serious conditions. Liver-enzyme effects can last after stopping. It is not a casual daily product.",
